WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.728
This is an original tabletop built from the visible Week 15 school plan. It is not the school’s hidden assessment station, official scoring sheet or Moodle quiz. Do not enter it as a result in the school system.
这是根据可见第15周计划编写的原创桌面演练，不是学校隐藏的考核站点、官方评分表或Moodle测验。不要把它作为成绩录入学校系统。

00:00:13.728 --> 00:00:25.512
Have the current adult and pediatric job aids open. The timer is a learning constraint, not a reason to skip safety, alter the algorithm or invent a missing observation.
应打开当前成人和儿童工作卡。计时是学习约束，不是忽略安全、修改算法或编造缺失观察的理由。

00:00:25.512 --> 00:00:39.480
For a small crew, functions may be combined as the incident plan directs. The exercise lead announces who is coordinating each function and where reports go; learners do not create a second command structure.
小团队可按事件计划合并职能。演练负责人要宣布每项职能由谁协调、向谁报告；学习者不能另建第二套指挥结构。

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:52.512
Rotate roles only at an explicit handoff. The next person repeats the current hazards, patient count, triage totals, unit status, destinations and open requests before accepting the role.
只有在明确交接后才能轮换角色。接任者应复述当前危险、患者数、各类检伤总数、车辆状态、目的地和待办请求，再确认接任。

00:00:52.512 --> 00:01:07.608
A high-speed collision involves four vehicles on a two-lane highway. Dispatch reports at least twelve people, including children. One access road is partly blocked, the count is still an estimate and two occupants have not been located.
一场高速碰撞涉及双车道公路上的四辆车。调度报告至少12人，其中包括儿童。一个通道部分受阻，人数仍是估算，另有两名乘员尚未找到。

00:01:07.608 --> 00:01:24.816
Your team has one ambulance at the scene. A second unit is delayed by traffic. The scenario is designed to test the system, not to reward a fast diagnosis: announce the capacity problem, request appropriate resources and use the current incident structure.
现场只有一辆救护车，第二辆因交通受阻。情景旨在检验系统协同，而非奖励快速诊断：要报告能力不足、请求适当资源，并使用当前事件架构。

00:01:24.816 --> 00:02:08.472
In this fictional rehearsal you are the assigned exercise incident lead. Practice report: Dispatch, Unit twenty-one. Major incident declared at Highway eight and Cedar Road: a four-vehicle high-speed collision. At least twelve patients reported, including children; two occupants remain unlocated. Individual conditions are not yet confirmed. One access lane is partly blocked; no additional hazard has been confirmed. Request additional ambulances and fire-service traffic and extrication support through dispatch. Unit twenty-one will update after the first count. This exercise role does not grant real incident-command authority.
本次虚构排练中，你受派担任演练事件负责人。练习通报：调度，21号车。8号公路与Cedar Road交叉口已宣布重大事件，为四车高速碰撞。报告至少12名患者，包括儿童；两名乘员仍未找到，个体状况尚未确认。一条通道部分受阻，目前未确认其他危险。请通过调度增派救护车及消防交通、解困支援。完成第一轮统计后21号车会更新。此演练角色不授予真实事件指挥权限。

00:02:08.472 --> 00:02:22.776
The location and unit number are fictional training details. In a live response, use the actual location, observed hazards and dispatched resources. Never repeat the practice script as a real report.
地点和车辆编号均为虚构训练资料。真实响应时应使用实际地点、观察到的危险和调派资源。切勿将练习脚本直接当作真实通报。

00:02:22.776 --> 00:02:46.320
Use the current adult chart for each fictional card. Cards B through F cannot walk on command. A is Minor; B is Deceased after airway positioning fails to restore breathing; C, D and E are Immediate at their first matching branch. F is Delayed because the earlier breathing and perfusion branches are negative and the command is followed.
对每张虚构卡片使用成人现行图表，B至F均不能按指令行走。A为Minor；B在摆正气道仍未恢复呼吸后标为Deceased；C、D、E在各自第一个符合条件的分支进入Immediate。F在前面呼吸与灌注分支均为阴性，且能遵从指令后进入Delayed。

00:02:46.320 --> 00:03:03.576
A tag is a rapid priority message, not a definitive diagnosis. In practice, use the exact local labels, required patient identifier and movement instructions. If the card leaves a key finding out, ask for clarification rather than guessing.
标签是快速优先级信息，不是确诊。实际练习中应使用准确的本地名称、患者编号和移动指示。若卡片缺少关键发现，应请求澄清而不是猜测。

00:03:03.576 --> 00:03:18.384
The posted BCEHS START aids set a target of 30 seconds per patient. Keep the chart visible until the sequence is reliable. The aim is a consistent first pass, not guessing faster or compressing a necessary branch.
BCEHS张贴的START工作卡设定每名患者30秒的目标。熟练前应保持图表可见。目标是一致完成第一轮，而不是更快猜测或省略必要分支。

00:03:18.384 --> 00:03:33.408
The school may observe time, category, tag and communication separately. Record each honestly. Finishing inside the target does not prove accuracy, and a correct tag does not excuse an unsafe approach.
学校可能分别观察用时、类别、标签和沟通。应如实记录。时间达标不能证明准确，标签正确也不能弥补不安全的接近方式。

00:03:33.408 --> 00:03:47.520
After the first six cards, the scribe reports the count and the triage leader confirms it against visible tags. The two unlocated occupants remain “not yet found,” not silently dropped from the incident picture.
完成前六张卡后，记录员报告人数，检伤负责人对照可见标签确认。两名尚未找到的乘员仍应记为“尚未找到”，不能从事件态势中悄悄删掉。

00:03:47.520 --> 00:04:01.680
When a patient moves or is reassigned, update the incident’s approved tracking method. If the digital system is unavailable, use the fallback specified by command rather than creating a separate undocumented process.
患者移动或任务调整时，应更新事件批准的追踪方式。若数字系统不可用，应使用指挥指定的备用流程，而不是另建未记录的流程。

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:16.968
A bus is found down an embankment, and six children are brought to the safe sorting area. Use JumpSTART as assigned by the exercise lead. Keep walking ability, respiratory branch, pulse and AVPU in their correct order.
在路堤下发现一辆校车，六名儿童被带到安全分流区。按演练负责人的指示使用JumpSTART。按正确顺序判断行走能力、呼吸分支、脉搏和AVPU。

00:04:16.968 --> 00:04:30.120
This additional group changes patient count, staff needs and the urgency of the next radio update. The triage lead informs command; the team does not begin an uncoordinated transport surge.
新患者群改变了人数、人员需求和下一次无线电更新的紧迫性。检伤负责人通知指挥；团队不能未经协调就开始集中转运。

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:58.368
Cards B through D are non-walking; C and D are breathing spontaneously. A enters the Minor walking branch. B remains apneic after airway positioning but has a pulse; continued apnea after the chart’s five breaths leads to Deceased on this tool. C is Immediate because the breathing rate is above forty-five. D is Delayed after the relevant breathing, pulse and appropriate pain-response findings.
B至D均不能行走，C及D有自主呼吸。A进入Minor行走分支。B摆正气道后仍无呼吸，但有脉搏；按图给予五次人工呼吸后仍无呼吸，按该工具标为Deceased。C呼吸频率超过45，进入Immediate。D依据相应呼吸、脉搏及对疼痛的适当反应，进入Delayed。

00:04:58.368 --> 00:05:13.656
Do not use the adult respiratory threshold, a full neurological scale or an age rule recalled from a textbook. If the child’s communication or developmental needs make the tool uncertain, request the appropriate secondary review through command.
不要使用成人呼吸阈值、完整神经量表或从教材记来的年龄规则。若儿童的沟通或发育需求使工具应用不确定，应通过指挥请求适当的二次评估。

00:05:13.656 --> 00:05:30.720
The second update should not repeat the original report word for word. State that a bus has been found, six additional children are accounted for, two vehicle occupants remain unlocated, access is still partly restricted and the second ambulance is delayed.
第二次更新不应逐字重复初次报告。应说明已找到校车，新增六名儿童已纳入统计，两名车辆乘员仍未找到，通道仍受限制，第二辆救护车仍延误。

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:42.720
Ask command to confirm the next resource or traffic action and report whether transport destinations can accept the current mix. Mark estimates clearly and set the next update trigger.
请求指挥确认下一项资源或交通行动，并报告接收医院能否接纳当前患者组合。明确标注估算，并设定下一次更新触发条件。

00:05:42.720 --> 00:06:00.144
In the next run, a child previously sorted as Delayed has a reliable respiratory rate of 48 per minute. Do not preserve the earlier category because it is already on the tag. Reassess using JumpSTART and update the priority according to the current chart.
下一轮中，先前分为Delayed的儿童复测到可信的呼吸频率为每分钟48次。不能因标签已贴好就保留旧类别。应使用JumpSTART重新评估，并按当前图表更新优先级。

00:06:00.144 --> 00:06:13.416
The update belongs to the incident system: tell the triage lead, receiving treatment function and transport coordinator as the plan requires. Keep the earlier value and the new value distinguishable in the record.
这项更新属于事件系统：按计划通知检伤负责人、治疗职能和转运协调员。记录中要区分此前测值和新测值。

00:06:13.416 --> 00:06:28.992
The transport lead does not simply choose the nearest facility. The role coordinates the plan, unit availability, route and receiving capacity; dispatch and command receive updates so vehicles do not stack at one access point.
转运负责人不能只选择最近的医院。该角色要协调计划、车辆可用性、路线和接收能力，并向调度和指挥更新，避免车辆堆积在同一通道。

00:06:28.992 --> 00:06:41.712
Use the local patient identifier and authorized transport log. A head count alone is not enough to reconnect the triage category, the patient and the destination after the scene changes.
应使用本地患者编号和获准转运记录。仅有总人数不足以在现场变化后重新关联检伤类别、患者和目的地。

00:06:41.712 --> 00:06:58.320
The school asks learners to rotate command in the Sunday exercise. Make the rotation an observable handoff rather than a silent change: the incoming leader receives the current picture and accepts it, then command identifies the new contact to the crews.
学校要求学习者在周日演练中轮换指挥。要把轮换做成可观察的交接，而不是悄悄换人：接任负责人接收并确认当前态势后，指挥再向各组宣布新的联系人。

00:06:58.320 --> 00:07:08.304
If the handoff is interrupted, pause the role change and ask for the missing part. Do not assume the new lead heard a critical hazard or transport constraint.
若交接被打断，应暂停角色变更并补齐缺失内容。不要假设新负责人已经听到关键危险或转运限制。

00:07:08.304 --> 00:07:22.560
Begin with the timeline and observed actions. Ask what the team expected, what actually happened, which update changed the plan and whether the right role received it. Keep the discussion specific enough that another observer could verify it.
先回顾时间线和观察到的行动。询问团队原本预期什么、实际发生什么、哪条更新改变了计划，以及正确角色是否收到。讨论要具体到另一位观察者也能核实。

00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:38.592
Look for system conditions as well as individual decisions: blocked access, noisy radio traffic, duplicate tasking, missing tags, transport delays or unclear role transfer. End with one change and a repeated scenario to test it.
既要看个人决策，也要看系统条件：通道受阻、无线电噪音、重复派工、标签缺失、转运延误或角色交接不清。最后提出一项改变，并用重复情景检验。

00:07:38.592 --> 00:07:53.688
A trainee may feel distress after assigning different priorities to patients who all need help. Invite a concise reflection on the decision and the resource constraint; do not ask the learner to prove that they cared by disclosing personal details.
学习者可能会因给同样需要帮助的患者分配不同优先级而感到痛苦。可以邀请其简要反思决策和资源限制；不要要求学习者披露私人细节来证明其有同理心。

00:07:53.688 --> 00:08:08.232
A fair process uses the agreed tool consistently, communicates uncertainty and asks for review when a case does not fit. The category is a temporary operational message, not a judgment of worth or a guarantee of outcome.
公平流程要求一致使用约定工具、传达不确定性，并在病例不适用时请求复核。类别是临时操作信息，不是价值判断或结局保证。

00:08:08.232 --> 00:08:24.144
Extended incidents require role coverage, relief, hydration, food and rest to be planned by the appropriate command and logistics functions. Do not invent fixed shift durations or rotations; use the actual local incident plan.
长时间事件需要由相应指挥和后勤职能规划岗位覆盖、替班、饮水、食物和休息。不要自行规定固定班次或轮换时间；应使用真实本地事件计划。

00:08:24.144 --> 00:08:42.888
A strong emotional response can occur even when a team followed the plan. Support should be respectful and voluntary. If distress continues or interferes with sleep, safety or daily functioning, use the available professional support route rather than relying on a class debrief alone.
即使团队遵循计划，也可能产生强烈情绪反应。支持应尊重且自愿。若困扰持续，或影响睡眠、安全或日常功能，应使用可用专业支持渠道，而不只依赖课堂复盘。

00:08:42.888 --> 00:08:57.504
This original checklist supports rehearsal. It does not assign an official pass mark, replace the instructor’s current scoring form or establish clinical competence. Keep any final performance record in the school’s required format.
这份原创清单用于练习，不设定官方及格分数，不替代教官当前评分表，也不证明临床能力。最终表现记录应使用学校要求的格式。

00:08:57.504 --> 00:09:10.440
After the run, give one observed strength, one specific gap and one repeatable next action. Then rerun the changed segment so the learner can demonstrate the repair rather than only describe it.
演练后反馈一项观察到的优势、一项具体差距和一个可重复的下一步行动。再重演已改变的片段，让学习者实际展示修正，而不只是在口头上描述。
